    "long_instructions": "## Exploring Temperature\r\n\r\n**Temperature** is one of the values you can control once a language model has been trained. Let's experiment with it and see if we can tell what it does.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n**Temperature** controls the randomness of how a model responds.\r\n- ⬇️ lower temperatures create less random, less creative responses\r\n- ⬆️ higher temperatures create more random, more creative responses\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### Do This\r\n\r\n1) Have a 3-4 message conversation with the chatbot about a book or movie or band you like.\r\n2) Change the temperature to a high value like 0.8 **Press the <code style=\"color:white; background-color:#7435b2\">Update</code> button!**\r\n3) Have another 3-4 message conversation about the same topic. Do you notice a difference in the type of responses?\r\n4) Change the temperature to a low value like 0.2 **Press the <code style=\"color:white; background-color:#7435b2\">Update</code> button!**\r\n5) Have another 3-4 message conversation about the same topic. Do you notice a difference in the type of responses?\r\n\r\n**Discuss:** How were the responses different for higher temperatures? Lower temperatures?",
